{"uid":"8fc7091abe6873cc","name":"test_a_later_cure_pass_reuses_the_retake_task_and_never_reopens_the_cure","fullName":"tests.test_cure_invalidates#test_a_later_cure_pass_reuses_the_retake_task_and_never_reopens_the_cure","historyId":"848812ec71c6461226f265de09a58a46","time":{"start":1791959551102,"stop":1791959551107,"duration":5},"description":"Route 1 of the same misclassification, plus Change 2's reuse. A\n    re-take task's own `successCriteria` names its path verbatim and it\n    `dependsOn`s its cure task, so from pass 2 on it satisfied \"criteria\n    names the path AND a non-empty dependsOn\" and was matched as the plan's\n    own lane-evidence record -- which re-opened its cure task and wrote a\n    cure-to-cure edge (`selfdev-v022`: `cure-01-01.dependsOn ==\n    ['cure-01-02']`). Now the re-take is invisible to that recognition and\n    the path re-uses that ONE row at the new cure's tree instead.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Route 1 of the same misclassification, plus Change 2's reuse. A<br />\nre-take task's own <code>successCriteria</code> names its path verbatim and it<br />\n<code>dependsOn</code>s its cure task, so from pass 2 on it satisfied &quot;criteria<br />\nnames the path AND a non-empty dependsOn&quot; and was matched as the plan's<br />\nown lane-evidence record -- which re-opened its cure task and wrote a<br />\ncure-to-cure edge (<code>selfdev-v022</code>: <code>cure-01-01.dependsOn == ['cure-01-02']</code>). Now the re-take is invisible to that recognition and<br />\nthe path re-uses that ONE row at the new cure's tree instead.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791959389113,"stop":1791959389113,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{